From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not abandon Repo setup over a persistence cache

Repo's constructor works out where an on-disk persistence cache would go, and
returns early if it cannot place one:

    std::string app_data_path = AppDataDir(database_path.c_str(), true, &err);
    if (app_data_path.empty()) {
      logger_->LogError("Could not initialize persistence: ...");
      return;
    }

The return is before server_sync_tree_ is constructed, and nothing else sets
it. Repo stays alive with a null member, DatabaseInternal::initialized() is
app_ != nullptr so the Database is handed out as usable, and the first write
dereferences it:

    Repo::SetValue
      mov 0x108(%rsi),%rcx     ; this->server_sync_tree_
      mov (%rcx),%rax          ; access violation
      call *0x58(%rax)         ; SyncTree::ApplyUserOverwrite

Reached on Windows against the Realtime Database emulator. The url there is
http://127.0.0.1:9000/?ns=<project>, so database_path ends in the segments
"127.0.0.1:9000" and "?ns=<project>". AppDataDir creates each one under
%LOCALAPPDATA%, and ':' and '?' are reserved in NTFS paths, so the create
fails. Linux and macOS allow both characters in a filename and never notice.

The directory is only read by CreatePersistenceManager a few lines later,
under if (persistence_enabled_). With persistence off -- the default -- setup
is abandoned over a path nothing goes on to use.

So work it out only when there is a cache to put there, and let a cache that
cannot be placed fall back to keeping none. Every path through the block now
constructs the sync tree. The two earlier returns in the same block, for a
missing package_name and an empty url, left the same null member and are
folded into the same fallback.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Carried by firebase_ffi, where the set is maintained:
https://github.com/jwinarske/firebase_ffi/tree/main/packages/firebase_ffi/patches/firebase-cpp-sdk
---
--- a/database/src/desktop/core/repo.cc	2026-09-07 09:00:45.496194360 -0700
+++ b/database/src/desktop/core/repo.cc	2026-09-07 09:01:15.576509913 -0700
@@ -474,48 +474,49 @@
 
   // Set up server sync tree.
   {
-    // The path path to the on-disk persistence cache, relative to the
-    // per-application data directory.
-    std::string database_path;
-
-    const char* package_name = database_->GetApp()->options().package_name();
-    if (!package_name) {
-      logger_->LogError("Could not initialize persistence: No package_name.");
-      return;
-    }
-
-    if (url_.empty()) {
-      logger_->LogError("Could not initialize persistence: No database url.");
-      return;
-    }
-
-    // Skip past the https:// or http://
-    auto start = url_.find("//") + strlen("//");
-    std::string url_domain = url_.substr(start);
-
-    database_path += package_name;
-    database_path += "/";
-    database_path += url_domain;
-
-    std::string app_data_path_error;
-    std::string app_data_path =
-        AppDataDir(database_path.c_str(),
-                   /* should_create = */ true, &app_data_path_error);
-    if (app_data_path.empty()) {
-      logger_->LogError(
-          "Could not initialize persistence: App data directory error: %s",
-          app_data_path_error.c_str());
-      return;
+    // Where the on-disk persistence cache goes, relative to the
+    // per-application data directory. Only worked out when there is a cache to
+    // put there: with persistence off nothing below reads this, and failing to
+    // place a directory no one uses is not a reason to abandon setup.
+    std::string app_data_path;
+    if (persistence_enabled_) {
+      std::string database_path;
+      const char* package_name = database_->GetApp()->options().package_name();
+      if (!package_name) {
+        logger_->LogError("Could not initialize persistence: No package_name.");
+      } else if (url_.empty()) {
+        logger_->LogError("Could not initialize persistence: No database url.");
+      } else {
+        // Skip past the https:// or http://
+        auto start = url_.find("//") + strlen("//");
+        std::string url_domain = url_.substr(start);
+
+        database_path += package_name;
+        database_path += "/";
+        database_path += url_domain;
+
+        std::string app_data_path_error;
+        app_data_path = AppDataDir(database_path.c_str(),
+                                   /* should_create = */ true,
+                                   &app_data_path_error);
+        if (app_data_path.empty()) {
+          logger_->LogError(
+              "Could not initialize persistence: App data directory error: %s",
+              app_data_path_error.c_str());
+        } else {
+          logger_->LogDebug("app_data_path: %s", app_data_path.c_str());
+        }
+      }
     }
 
-    logger_->LogDebug("app_data_path: %s", app_data_path.c_str());
-
     // Set up write tree.
     auto pending_write_tree = std::make_unique<WriteTree>();
 
-    // Set up persistence manager
+    // Set up persistence manager. A cache that could not be placed falls back
+    // to keeping none: the error above says why, and returning instead would
+    // leave server_sync_tree_ null for every later call to dereference.
     std::unique_ptr<PersistenceManagerInterface> persistence_manager;
-    if (persistence_enabled_) {
+    if (persistence_enabled_ && !app_data_path.empty()) {
       persistence_manager =
           CreatePersistenceManager(app_data_path.c_str(), logger_);
     } else {
